    "overviewDetail": "Mauritius has positioned itself as one of the most attractive offshore and international business destinations, particularly for companies looking to expand into Africa and beyond. With a robust financial services sector, a stable political environment, and a well-regulated legal system based on English common law and French civil law, Mauritius offers both flexibility and credibility for global businesses.\n\nThe country is widely recognised for its Global Business Company (GBC) structures, which are commonly used for cross-border investments, holding entities, and fund management. Its network of double taxation avoidance agreements (DTAAs) across Africa, Asia, and Europe enhances its appeal as a tax-efficient jurisdiction. Regulatory bodies such as the Financial Services Commission (FSC) ensure compliance while maintaining ease of doing business.\n\nMauritius continues to evolve beyond traditional financial services, with growth in fintech, fintech regulation, and digital innovation. Combined with cost efficiency, skilled talent, and strong connectivity, Mauritius remains a compelling choice for startups, SMEs, and multinational corporations seeking international expansion.\n",
